                        "glosses": [
                            "One of two species of acanthus, Acanthus spinosus or Acanthus mollis; bear's breech."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "uncountable"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "11bbb8ab-482f-4a5a-9ce7-5f147db2bf47",
                                "sense_id": "22d4c33f-d1c1-3c80-b927-24baa8b81591",
                                "text": "The roots and leaves of brankursine abound with a soft, insipid, mucilaginous substance; which is readily extracted by coction or infusion in water, and remains entire upon evaporating the liquid."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "b6907362-ea4e-4de2-9a16-ab25ba42acb9",
                                "sense_id": "22d4c33f-d1c1-3c80-b927-24baa8b81591",
                                "text": "The editor of the Wirtemberg Pharmacopoeia observes, that the leaves of acanthus brankursine or bears breech , give a more durable green tincture to spirit than those of any other herb."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "0a69e4ff-65f1-46b7-945d-4b7353ba6d6c",
                                "sense_id": "22d4c33f-d1c1-3c80-b927-24baa8b81591",
                                "text": "The soil of Maremma was treacherous as Iago, and, though she made no count of it, her days were full of danger as the timid snipe's for whom the fox waits in the brushwood, and the muzzle of the gun slips through the reeds, and the hawk watches above the air, and the dog steals through the fennel and brankursine ."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
